# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CCE — Capital Control Engine
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Documentation ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The full spec set is PUBLIC. It is the strongest part of the repository:
# twelve numbered safety invariants, 113 numbered requirements, every
# formula with its units and annualisation, and an implementation plan that
# records what actually went wrong rather than only what was intended.
#
# Two exceptions below — a scratch file and the private working notes.
# Everything else ships.
# (nothing excluded — readme_fintech.md is the hackathon brief and gives
# a reader the problem CCE was built against, so it ships too.)

# ── Deployment ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.vercel/

# ── Working screenshots ──────────────────────────────────────
# Demo captures for the deck. Kept out of the repo: they are large,
# they go stale the moment a threshold moves, and the README/pitch page
# already carry the numbers. Anything a reader needs to SEE should be
# reproducible by running the app, not pinned as a PNG.
website images/

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
# ...but the TEMPLATE is committed: a fresh clone otherwise has no
# record of which variables exist, and the constitution requires it.
# It holds no secrets — only defaults and a commented-out placeholder.
!.env.example
# Streamlit: secrets stay out, config.toml ships — it carries the theme and
# the server settings the deployed app needs, and holds nothing sensitive.
.streamlit/secrets.toml
!.streamlit/config.toml
*.pem
*.key

# ── Database (recreatable from migrations) ───────────────────
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
data/cce.db

# ── Market data ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# raw/ and processed/ are regenerable; cache/ is COMMITTED so the
# demo is reproducible and runs with no network. See docs/02 §8.
data/raw/
data/processed/
!data/cache/
!data/cache/**

